\f0\b\fs26 \cf0 Clean List of Steps to Rebuild the Staging Environment\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\sl276\slmult1\sb240\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs22 \cf0 Below is a streamlined list of steps to consistently rebuild the staging environment for your app. These steps assume you\'92re starting from a clean slate (e.g., after deleting the previous staging backend environment) and need to redeploy and configure everything.\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\sl276\slmult1\sb240\sa40\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Step 1: Set the Staging Environment Variable During Initial Deployment\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\sl276\slmult1\sb240\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf0 The AMPLIFY_ENV environment variable ensures the correct redirect URIs are used for the staging environment in amplify/auth/resource.ts.\
\pard\tx360\tx1080\pardeftab720\li1080\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	1.	}1.	
\f0\b Go to the Amplify Console
\f1\b0 :\
\pard\tx1080\tx1800\pardeftab720\li1800\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl1\cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9675 	Navigate to the Amplify Console > Your app (hiresmart) > 
\f0\b App settings
\f1\b0  > 
\f0\b Environment variables
\f1\b0 .\
\pard\tx360\tx1080\pardeftab720\li1080\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	2.	}2.	
\f0\b Set the Environment Variable
\f1\b0 :\
\pard\tx1080\tx1800\pardeftab720\li1800\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl1\cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9675 	Click 
\f0\b Manage variables
\f1\b0 .\
{\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9675 	Add or update the following environment variable:\
\pard\tx1800\tx2520\pardeftab720\li2520\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl2\cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9632 	
\f0\b Key
\f1\b0 : AMPLIFY_ENV\
{\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9632 	
\f0\b Value
\f1\b0 : staging\
{\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9632 	
\f0\b Apply to
\f1\b0 : 
\f0\b staging
\f1\b0  branch\
\pard\tx1080\tx1800\pardeftab720\li1800\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl1\cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9675 	Save the changes.\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\sl276\slmult1\sb240\sa40\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 {\listtext	3.	}Step 2: Immediately Set the Secrets Required for the App After Staging Deployment Begins\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\sl276\slmult1\sb240\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b0 \cf0 {\listtext	4.	}The app requires Google OAuth secrets (GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID and GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET) for federated authentication in Cognito. These must be set as soon as the staging deployment starts to ensure the Cognito User Pool is configured correctly.\
\pard\tx360\tx1080\pardeftab720\li1080\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	1.	}1.	
\f0\b Go to the Amplify Console
\f1\b0 :\
\pard\tx1080\tx1800\pardeftab720\li1800\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl1\cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9675 	Navigate to the Amplify Console > Your app (hiresmart) > 
\f0\b App settings
\f1\b0  > 
\f0\b Secrets
\f1\b0 .\
\pard\tx360\tx1080\pardeftab720\li1080\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	2.	}2.	
\f0\b Set the Secrets
\f1\b0 :\
\pard\tx1080\tx1800\pardeftab720\li1800\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl1\cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9675 	Click 
\f0\b Manage secrets
\f1\b0 .\
{\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9675 	Add or update the following secrets:\
\pard\tx1800\tx2520\pardeftab720\li2520\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl2\cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9632 	
\f0\b Name
\f1\b0 : GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID\
\pard\tx2520\tx3240\pardeftab720\li3240\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl3\cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9632 	
\f0\b Value
\f1\b0 : <your-google-client-id> (replace with your actual Google OAuth Client ID)\
{\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9632 	
\f0\b Apply to
\f1\b0 : 
\f0\b staging
\f1\b0  branch\
\pard\tx1800\tx2520\pardeftab720\li2520\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl2\cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9632 	
\f0\b Name
\f1\b0 : GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET\
\pard\tx2520\tx3240\pardeftab720\li3240\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl3\cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9632 	
\f0\b Value
\f1\b0 : <your-google-client-secret> (replace with your actual Google OAuth Client Secret)\
{\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9632 	
\f0\b Apply to
\f1\b0 : 
\f0\b staging
\f1\b0  branch\
\pard\tx1080\tx1800\pardeftab720\li1800\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl1\cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9675 	Save the secrets.\
{\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9675 	
\f0\b Timing Note
\f1\b0 : Set these secrets immediately after triggering the staging deployment to ensure the Cognito User Pool configuration in amplify/auth/resource.ts can access them during the build.\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\sl276\slmult1\sb240\sa40\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 {\listtext	3.	}Step 3: Update Google Console with the New Authorized JavaScript Origins URL\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\sl276\slmult1\sb240\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b0 \cf0 {\listtext	4.	}The Google OAuth configuration requires the Authorized JavaScript origins to match the staging environment\'92s URL.\
\pard\tx360\tx1080\pardeftab720\li1080\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	1.	}1.	
\f0\b Get the Staging URL
\f1\b0 :\
\pard\tx1080\tx1800\pardeftab720\li1800\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl1\cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9675 	The staging URL is: https://staging.d1mjhvpisz36hi.amplifyapp.com.\
\pard\tx360\tx1080\pardeftab720\li1080\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	2.	}2.	
\f0\b Go to the Google Cloud Console
\f1\b0 :\
\pard\tx1080\tx1800\pardeftab720\li1800\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl1\cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9675 	Navigate to the Google Cloud Console > 
\f0\b APIs & Services
\f1\b0  > 
\f0\b Credentials
\f1\b0 .\
{\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9675 	Find your OAuth 2.0 Client ID (the one used for GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID).\
\pard\tx360\tx1080\pardeftab720\li1080\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	3.	}3.	
\f0\b Update Authorized JavaScript Origins
\f1\b0 :\
\pard\tx1080\tx1800\pardeftab720\li1800\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl1\cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9675 	Edit the OAuth 2.0 Client ID.\
{\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9675 	Under 
\f0\b Authorized JavaScript origins
\f1\b0 , add:\
\pard\tx1800\tx2520\pardeftab720\li2520\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl2\cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9632 	https://staging.d1mjhvpisz36hi.amplifyapp.com\
\pard\tx1080\tx1800\pardeftab720\li1800\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl1\cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9675 	Save the changes.\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\sl276\slmult1\sb240\sa40\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 {\listtext	4.	}Step 4: Update Google Console with the New Cognito Domain for Authorized Redirect URIs\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\sl276\slmult1\sb240\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b0 \cf0 {\listtext	5.	}The Google OAuth configuration requires the Authorized redirect URIs to match the Cognito User Pool\'92s callback URL, which includes the Cognito domain. Since the Cognito User Pool is recreated each time you rebuild the staging environment, you\'92ll need to update this URI.\
\pard\tx360\tx1080\pardeftab720\li1080\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	1.	}1.	
\f0\b Get the New Cognito Domain
\f1\b0 :\
\pard\tx1080\tx1800\pardeftab720\li1800\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl1\cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9675 	After the staging deployment completes, go to AWS Management Console > 
\f0\b Cognito
\f1\b0  > 
\f0\b User Pools
\f1\b0 .\
{\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9675 	Find the new User Pool for the staging environment (e.g., us-west-2_<new-id>).\
{\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9675 	Go to 
\f0\b App integration
\f1\b0  > 
\f0\b Domain
\f1\b0 .\
{\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9675 	Note the Cognito domain (e.g., https://hiresmart-staging-<hash>.auth.us-west-2.amazoncognito.com).\
\pard\tx360\tx1080\pardeftab720\li1080\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	2.	}2.	
\f0\b Get the Callback URL
\f1\b0 :\
\pard\tx1080\tx1800\pardeftab720\li1800\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl1
\f2\fs20 \cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9675 
\f3 	
\f1\fs22 The callback URL for the Cognito User Pool is constructed as:\uc0\u8232 https://<cognito-domain>/oauth2/idpresponse\u8232 
\f3\fs20 \cf1 \uc0\u8232 
\f1\fs22 \cf0 For example:\uc0\u8232 https://hiresmart-staging-<hash>.auth.us-west-2.amazoncognito.com/oauth2/idpresponse\u8232 
\f3\fs20 \cf1 https://hiresmart-staging-<hash>.auth.us-west-2.amazoncognito.com/oauth2/idpresponse\
\pard\tx360\tx1080\pardeftab720\li1080\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f1\fs22 \cf0 {\listtext	3.	}3.	
\f0\b Go to the Google Cloud Console
\f1\b0 :\
\pard\tx1080\tx1800\pardeftab720\li1800\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl1\cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9675 	Navigate to the Google Cloud Console > 
\f0\b APIs & Services
\f1\b0  > 
\f0\b Credentials
\f1\b0 .\
{\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9675 	Find your OAuth 2.0 Client ID.\
\pard\tx360\tx1080\pardeftab720\li1080\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	4.	}4.	
\f0\b Update Authorized Redirect URIs
\f1\b0 :\
\pard\tx1080\tx1800\pardeftab720\li1800\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl1\cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9675 	Edit the OAuth 2.0 Client ID.\
{\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9675 	Under 
\f0\b Authorized redirect URIs
\f1\b0 , add the new callback URL:\
\pard\tx1800\tx2520\pardeftab720\li2520\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl2\cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9632 	https://hiresmart-staging-<hash>.auth.us-west-2.amazoncognito.com/oauth2/idpresponse\
\pard\tx1080\tx1800\pardeftab720\li1800\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl1\cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9675 	Save the changes.\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\sl276\slmult1\sb240\sa40\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 {\listtext	5.	}Step 5: Import the Test Data into the Staging DynamoDB Table\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\sl276\slmult1\sb240\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f1\b0 \cf0 {\listtext	6.	}After the deployment completes, import the test data into the staging DynamoDB table to populate it with the necessary data.\
\pard\tx360\tx1080\pardeftab720\li1080\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	1.	}1.	
\f0\b Identify the Staging DynamoDB Table
\f1\b0 :\
\pard\tx1080\tx1800\pardeftab720\li1800\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl1\cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9675 	Go to AWS Management Console > 
\f0\b DynamoDB
\f1\b0  > 
\f0\b Tables
\f1\b0 .\
{\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9675 	Find the table used by the staging environment (e.g., HireSmartItem-staging-<hash>).\
\pard\tx360\tx1080\pardeftab720\li1080\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	2.	}2.	
\f0\b Update the Script with the Staging Table Name
\f1\b0 :\
\pard\tx1080\tx1800\pardeftab720\li1800\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl1
\f2\fs20 \cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9675 
\f3 	
\f1\fs22 Open import_dynamodb_from_s3.mjs.\uc0\u8232 
\f3\fs20 \cf1 code ~/projects/hiresmart/import_dynamodb_from_s3.mjs\
\ls5\ilvl1
\f2 \cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9675 
\f3 	
\f1\fs22 Update the TABLE_NAME variable with the staging table name:\uc0\u8232 
\f3\fs20 \cf2 const\cf1  \cf3 TABLE_NAME\cf1  = \cf4 'HireSmartItem-staging-<hash>'\cf1 ; 
\f4\i \cf5 // Replace with your staging table name\
\pard\tx360\tx1080\pardeftab720\li1080\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\f1\i0\fs22 \cf0 {\listtext	3.	}3.	
\f0\b Run the Script
\f1\b0 :\
\pard\tx1080\tx1800\pardeftab720\li1800\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl1
\f2\fs20 \cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9675 
\f3 	
\f1\fs22 Run the script to import the data into the staging table:\uc0\u8232 node ~/projects/hiresmart/import_dynamodb_from_s3.mjs
\f3\fs20 \cf1 \
\pard\tx1080\tx1800\pardeftab720\li1800\fi-360\ri0\sl276\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl1
\f1\fs22 \cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}\uc0\u9675 	
